Give the HDMI port type the count of its supported resolutions

The table of video port types names the table of resolutions with a count of
0, "info available at runtime". RDK's device settings plug-in
(entservices-devicesettings) takes a port type's supported resolutions from
this table alone, so with 0 it has none, and the display settings service
answers getSupportedResolutions with an empty list. The count is set to that
of the table when the library is loaded. (A Raspberry Pi 4 with this release
of the hardware layer and that plug-in would have the same empty list; not
tried on one.)

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/dsVideoPort.c
+++ b/dsVideoPort.c
@@ -2913,4 +2913,14 @@
     }
     _preferredColorDepth = colorDepth;
     return dsERR_NONE;
+}
+
+/* tv-emu: the table of video port types (dsVideoPortSettingsData.c) names the
+ * table of resolutions with a count of 0. RDK's device settings plug-in takes
+ * a port type's supported resolutions from that table and nowhere else, so
+ * it had none, and the display settings service's list of supported
+ * resolutions was empty. The count is that of the table. */
+__attribute__((constructor)) static void tvemuCountSupportedResolutions(void)
+{
+    kVideoPortConfigs[0].numSupportedResolutions = (size_t)kResolutionsSettings_size;
 }
